# jmk-autoplay-hud 0.1.37 (AGPL-3.0, as this package). Ported from the Open-HMG wireless CarPlay + Android Auto mod
# (AGPL-3.0, author VysseCodes per its mod.json): https://github.com/Open-HMG/hmgapi-wireless-cp-aa, tag v2.2.0-rc.9,
# commit f657ca4, wireless-carplay-aa/recipes/carplay-core-frames-ef49c09b.recipe; the lines below are that file's,
# byte for byte. Its reason is upstream issue #25 / pull request #26 (AwsomeFox): a short Wi-Fi stall ends the CarPlay
# video stream for good. Here it is written to the file (lpatch, as the other recipes), only for the stock build whose
# md5 recipes/gates names, and put back with the other stock copies on uninstall.
# libCarPlayCore ef49c09b (US 260903, the Korean Ioniq 5's build): ProcessFrames waits 10 s for a video frame, not 200 ms (movs r7,#0 / movt r7,#0xffff -> movs r7,#10 / movt r7,#0), as carplay-core-wifi does on 260507; this build takes Wi-Fi sessions already. Listed first: on other builds its region doesn't match and nothing is written
# generated by mkrecipe.py from stock ef49c09b7ab5eb72298f9973443b66b3 -> patched 36c65d80ea46f833f84c7567f43ffc2b
# holds only hashes of the stock bytes and the new bytes written
id carplay-core-frames-ef49c09b
file /system/lib/libCarPlayCore.so
verify 0x1482a 42 f167a8b61d9bbfe2a86eb973668a8abd 18c301cd2a43825630dbb44810b3d7fd
patch 0x1483a 0a
patch 0x14840 c0f20007
